{"name":"Mountain Quail","hex":"#605b57","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mountain quail","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Oreortyx pictus, a small ground-dwelling bird in the New World quail family.","Ophrysia superciliosa"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mountain_quail"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mountain quail","blocks":[{"text":"The mountain quail is a small ground-dwelling bird in the New World quail family. This species is the only one in the genus Oreortyx, which is sometimes included in Callipepla. This is not appropriate, however, as the mountain quail's ancestors diverged from other New World quails earlier than the bobwhites, no later than 6 mya."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b9/Oreortyx_pictus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_quail","wikidata":"Q594810"},{"title":"Mountain","blocks":[{"text":"A mountain is an elevated portion of the surface of a planet, generally with steep sides that show significant exposed bedrock. Although there are no universally accepted definitions, a mountain is usually considered higher than a hill. By definition, mountains are often thought of as being a landform which is higher than 2,000 feet (610 m). It may either have a limited summit area or be a smaller plateau with high elevation and steep sides. A few mountains are isolated summits, but most occur in mountain ranges."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg/330px-Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain","wikidata":"Q8502"},{"title":"Quail","blocks":[{"text":"Quail is a collective name for several genera of mid-sized birds generally placed in the order Galliformes. The collective noun for a group of quail is a flock, covey, or bevy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Brown_Quail.jpg/330px-Brown_Quail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quail","wikidata":"Q6072584"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Oreortyx_pictus_90643590.jpg/500px-Oreortyx_pictus_90643590.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Oreortyx_pictus_90643590.jpg/1280px-Oreortyx_pictus_90643590.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Oreortyx_pictus_90643590.jpg/500px-Oreortyx_pictus_90643590.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOreortyx_pictus_90643590.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Oreortyx_pictus_189165978.jpg/500px-Oreortyx_pictus_189165978.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Oreortyx_pictus_189165978.jpg/1280px-Oreortyx_pictus_189165978.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Oreortyx_pictus_189165978.jpg/500px-Oreortyx_pictus_189165978.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOreortyx_pictus_189165978.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Oreortyx_pictusGBP14A.jpg/500px-Oreortyx_pictusGBP14A.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Oreortyx_pictusGBP14A.jpg/1280px-Oreortyx_pictu